From olivia.lau-cIpcPs7DjqbWs/AcZQh2Cw at public.gmane.org  Fri Aug 19 15:13:39 2011
From: olivia.lau-cIpcPs7DjqbWs/AcZQh2Cw at public.gmane.org (Olivia Lau)
Date: Fri, 19 Aug 2011 11:13:39 -0400
Subject: Re: sim () command error
In-Reply-To: <bd3a770351a92ea3e64bc7ff60710765@hu-berlin.de>
References: <bd3a770351a92ea3e64bc7ff60710765@hu-berlin.de>
Message-ID: <CAFKPR11z3u0N-53H2JzRDmmVmOM1yhu0jEURk=6eyRFpc79vUg@mail.gmail.com>

It turns out that the problem was in library incompatibilities.  Zsófia was
loading 20 packages at the beginning of the R session, with Zelig somewhere
in the middle.  Every time you load a library in R, the functions in that
library overwrite the functions of the same name in base R and previous R
libraries that you have loaded.

Suppose that there is a vcov function in the car library, and you load car
after you load Zelig. Then R will try to use the vcov function from car when
Zelig asks for a vcov function, and Zelig will not work.

Therefore, you should only load the libraries that you need at the beginning
of your R session, and you should always load Zelig last.  Zelig will load
additional libraries automatically as it needs them.  If you find that Zelig
is bombing when it had previously worked, quit your R session, restart, load
just the Zelig package, and start again.

There is no need to continually reinstall

Best,
Olivia

